    "question": "Randy had some money. Smith gave him another $200. Randy then gave Sally $1,200 and kept the rest. If Randy has $2000 left, how much money, in dollars, did Randy have at first?",
    "gold": "3000",
    "answer": "After Smith gave him $200, Randy had 2000+1200=<<2000+1200=3200>>3200 dollars.\nRandy had 3200-200=<<3200-200=3000>>3000 dollars at first.\n#### 3000"
  },
  "generation": {
    "text": "Let's denote the amount of money Randy had initially as \\( x \\) dollars.\n\n1. Smith gave Randy $200, so the amount of money Randy had after receiving the money from Smith is:\n   \\[\n   x + 200\n   \\]\n\n2. Randy then gave Sally $1,200, so the amount of money Randy had after giving $1,200 to Sally is:\n   \\[\n   (x + 200) - 1200 = x + 200 - 1200 = x - 1000\n   \\]\n\n3. According to the problem, after these transactions, Randy has $2000 left. Therefore, we can set up the following equation:\n   \\[\n   x - 1000 = 2000\n   \\]\n\n4. To find \\( x \\), we solve the equation by adding 1000 to both sides:\n   \\[\n   x = 2000 + 1000 = 3000\n   \\]\n\nSo, the amount of money Randy had at first is \\(\\boxed{3000}\\).",
